    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="General Relativity&#x27;s central insight is that gravity is not a force propagating through space, but the curvature of spacetime itself -- massive objects don&#x27;t pull on other objects, they bend the geometry that other objects move through in a straight line (a geodesic). Restricting the Schwarzschild metric to a constant-time, equatorial (\theta=\pi/2) slice leaves a curved 2D spatial geometry with proper length element">

